I stiffened the coverage and pushed in only when the pressure rises: locked S08 so Dinu’s objection hits like a wall, shortened Nimal’s reaction into a tighter CU, and used slow, motivated pushes on both men instead of that gentle drift. I brought the roof rain closer and drier around the faces, and laid a barely-there low rumble under L4 so the personal turn tightens without drowning the words. Net effect: less air between beats, more eye-to-eye squeeze.

